quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  62,1,"Whatever is in the heavens glorifies Allah, and whatever is on the earth, the Sovereign, the Most Holy, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise."
  62,2,"He is the One Who sent among the unlettered people a Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) from among themselves, who recites His revelations to them, purifies them (spiritually) and teaches them the Book and wisdom. Indeed, they had previously been in clear error,"
  62,3,"along with others among them who have not yet joined them. And He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise."
  62,4,That is Allah’s grace. He grants it to whomever He pleases. And Allah is the Lord of Mighty Grace.
  62,5,The example of those entrusted with the Torah but failed to carry this (trust) is like that of a donkey carrying books. How evil is the example of the people who reject Allah’s revelations? And Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.
  62,6,"Say: ‘O Jews! If you claim that you are Allah’s chosen friends, leaving all other people aside, then long for death, if you are truthful.’"
  62,7,Yet they will never long for it because of what (deeds) their hands have sent forth. And Allah is All-Knowing of the wrongdoers.
  62,8,"Say: ‘Indeed, the death you are running away from will surely encounter you. Then you will be returned to the Knower of the Unseen and the seen, and He will inform you of what you used to do.’"
